From b4f937ff6b25ad0382ccee3b241080218ed46d26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:09:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 40/60] Muse Spark: two ranks (TP=2) in the decode forward and
 tf-muse m1

Each rank runs its 64 query heads / 8 KV heads, its latent half of pre_expert_proj and post_expert_proj and its
half of every expert's width. Four fp32 all-gathers a layer, summed in rank order inside the kernels that
consume them: o_proj partials (post-attention gate), the latent halves (fp16, read in place by the latent norm),
the experts' down partials (the per-expert norm needs each expert's whole output), post_expert_proj partials
(post-ffn gate); the head's uneven 128-row block slices are gathered at the wider rank's stride. tf-muse m1 opens
a TP session when TF_TP_WORLD is set; rank 0 writes the dumps. One-GPU bits unchanged (the 2-layer logits are
byte-equal to the previous build's); the two-rank path has not run yet (both GPUs busy).
